The system is formed initially by a number of moles of $n_\ce{H2}^0$ and $n_\ce{I2}^0$, which I will consider equal, so $ n_\ce{H2}^0 = n_\ce{I2}^0 = n^0$. By stoichiometry we link the moles of the species to the extent of the reaction
\begin{align}
 n_\ce{H2} &= n^0 - \frac{1}{2}\xi \\
