where $I$ is the moment of inertia.
Then the rotational constant $B_{0} = \frac{\hbar^2}{2 I}$ (in units of energy) is introduced, so

\begin{align}
 E_{\mathrm{rot}} = B_{0} J ( J + 1 ) \ .
\end{align}

Thus

\begin{align}
 Q_{\mathrm{rot}} = \sum_{J=0}^{\infty}{(2J+1)\exp\left(-\frac{B_0 J(J+1)}{kT}\right)} \ ,
\end{align}

